'''dpi'''

# [[dots per inch]]
#:{{context|graphic design|typography}} DPI is used to describe the resolution number of dots per inch in a digital print and the printing resolution of a hard copy print dot gain; the increase in the size of the halftone dots during printing. This is caused by the spreading of ink on the surface of the media.. The DPI measurement of a printer often needs to be considerably higher than the pixels per inch (PPI) resolution of the image to produce similar-quality output.


